## Exact branch-product cover

Each physical pentagon face has 20 closed local branches: ten admissible cyclic gap orders times the two closed median sides, with the five rank-specific branch-adaptive closure secants already certified earlier in the theorem chain.

For every listed cell the verifier exact-certifies each locally impossible branch at faces 2 and 3. Any of the 400 branch products containing one of those branches is then already impossible. It exact-certifies every remaining product of locally feasible branches. This covers all 400 possible simultaneous branch choices at the two faces and excludes the reciprocal cell.

Across the 30 new cells the check uses 856 exact one-face branch certificates and 1,024 exact two-face product certificates, 1,880 certificates total. Of these, 1,770 have a strictly negative forced constant and 110 have forced constant zero. The largest denominator among active exact dual coefficients is

\[
3742297537070786996599355.
\]

Numerical LPs only locate candidate dual supports. Each accepted certificate is reconstructed and checked in exact rational arithmetic: inequality multipliers are nonnegative, strict weights sum to one, all 85 variable coefficients cancel exactly, equality multipliers are unrestricted, and the forced constant is nonpositive.

## Relation to the discovery scan

The fixed face-`(2,3)` discovery pass over the first 700 positions of the 4,944-cell one-face endpoint found 126 numerical candidate exclusions with no LP failures. The preceding committed two-face batches accounted for the first 60 candidates after removing overlap with earlier certificates. This step exactifies candidates 61 through 90 of that ordered discovery list. Their complete-angle indices are all larger than those in the prior face-`(2,3)` extension, so the 30 cells here are disjoint from all earlier exact two-face batches; the verifier also checks disjointness explicitly.

There remain 36 numerical candidates from that first-700 fixed-pair batch that are not counted until exactification is complete.

## Scope and next target

This is a necessary-condition reduction in the generic H6 branch. It does not prove any of the remaining 4,841 cells geometrically realizable and it does not cover reciprocal-collinearity walls.

The immediate next task is to exactify the remaining 36 face-`(2,3)` candidates from the first 700-cell block, then continue the same fixed-pair scan beyond position 700. After exhausting cheap two-face affine cuts, the surviving generic cells still must satisfy the fifteen independent complete reciprocal sine-law metric consistency equations. Reciprocal-collinearity walls remain a separate nongeneric branch.
